areer-high No. 41 in the live rankings, although the official rankings will not be released until the tournament is completed. Before this year, Tirante had never won more than six top-level matches in a season. He has now won 26 in 2026, including trips to the fourth round at the Masters tournaments in Rome and Montreal.\nHe has also become increasingly dangerous against highly ranked opponents. His Cincinnati victory over Djokovic followed wins against Ben Shelton and Taylor Fritz earlier this season. Tirante will now turn his attention to the US Open, where he has secured a place in the main draw. Singles play begins August 30 in New York.\nAfter arriving in Cincinnati as a player unfamiliar to many casual tennis fans, Tirante will enter the year’s final Grand Slam as one of Latin America’s most interesting players to watch.",
