        "image": "https://thoughtcatalog.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/you-are-loved-you-are-missed-and-you-will-never-be-forgotten-wladimir-klitschko.jpg?w=1536&h=768&crop=1",
        "full_content": "“You Are Loved, You Are Missed, And You Will Never Be Forgotten.” Wladimir Klitschko Honored Hayden Panettiere on What Would Have Been Her 37th Birthday\nHayden Panettiere would have turned 37 on Friday. She died August 16 at 36, found in cardiac arrest at a residence in Greenville, South Carolina, in what reports describe as an apparent overdose.\nWladimir Klitschko, the retired heavyweight champion she was engaged to and shared a daughter with, posted the tribute to X on the morning of her birthday. “Today is Hayden’s birthday,” he wrote. “Instead of celebrating the way we had planned, today we celebrate her life, her spirit, and the love she brought into this world.”\nThe two met around 2008 and got engaged in 2013. Their daughter, Kaya, was born in Hawaii in December 2014 and is now 11. Panettiere signed over full custody in 2018 while she was fighting addiction, and Kaya has since been raised by Klitschko, largely in Ukraine.\nHe turned the post into a request. “If you’re reading this, I ask just one thing: even if only for a moment, think about LOVE. Reach out to a friend. Forgive someone. Be kind.”\n“Love is a superpower,” he added. “Use it.”\nIt’s his second public statement since her death. On August 18 he called it “a time of profound shock and grief” and promised their daughter would grow up knowing exactly who her mother was.\nThank you for reading. Catch all of Thought Catalog’s latest on Facebook and our website.",
