        "title": "US senator denounces Trump’s 'disastrous' war on Iran",
        "link": "https://www.tehrantimes.com/news/529276/US-senator-denounces-Trump-s-disastrous-war-on-Iran",
        "source": "",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:38:57.180829+00:00",
        "image": "https://media.tehrantimes.com/d/t/2026/08/21/4/6141075.jpg?ts=1787324473646",
        "full_content": "US senator denounces Trump’s 'disastrous' war on Iran\nTEHRAN — Deepening political fracturing within the United States establishment has broken into the open, as senior American lawmakers increasingly characterize Washington’s ongoing hostilities against Iran as an unmitigated strategic catastrophe.\nIn a public rebuke reflecting widespread panic among American elites, US Senator Mark Warner, vice-chairman of the Senate Intelligence Committee, sharply criticized the White House’s warmongering campaign in West Asia. Taking to social media, the prominent lawmaker admitted that American forces are paying a crushing price for Washington’s strategic miscalculations.\n“Every day the Iran War stretches on, our servicemembers are at risk, our prices increase, and our national security readiness diminishes,” Warner confessed, acknowledging the severe economic turmoil and military exhaustion inflicted upon the United States by its own belligerence. Stripping away official rhetoric, Warner directly challenged the administration's reckless adventurism, demanding: “When will Trump walk away from this disastrous and deadly war?”\nWarner’s admission comes as political observers point to a long history of American imperial overreach in the region. For decades, Washington has operated under the delusion that illegal sanctions, covert subversion, and military threats could bend the sovereign will of the Iranian nation. From the foreign-backed 1953 coup that overthrew Iran's democratically elected government, to the criminal campaign of \"maximum pressure\" economic terrorism and the cowardly assassination of anti-terror icon General Qasem Soleimani, American foreign policy has consistently relied on coercion and lawlessness.\nYet, as the Iranian defensive forces continue to demonstrate unyielding strength, the limits of American power have been laid bare. Washington now finds itself bogged down in a conflict of its own making, facing skyrocketing domestic inflation, declining military readiness, and mounting international isolation.\nTehran has repeatedly reaffirmed that while it seeks no escalation, it will never hesitate to deliver a decisive and crushing response to any act of foreign aggression. Senator Warner’s stark warning confirms what regional experts have long asserted: Washington’s unilateralist ambitions in West Asia have collided with the firm reality of Iranian sovereignty. With internal political dissent intensifying and the economic burden becoming unbearable for ordinary Americans, the White House is running out of options in a war it can neither justify nor sustain.\n \n  ",
