ains while preserving an identity distinct from the LDP.\nBoth candidates favor continuing such policy-by-policy cooperation. But Hashimoto says the race should include debate over how the DPP deals with the ruling bloc, while Tamaki has pledged to retain his “solutions over confrontation” approach.\nThe winner will be chosen Sept. 6 through a 159-point vote, with 53 points each allocated to national lawmakers, local assembly members, and party members and supporters.",
