        "full_content": "The best Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold deals at launch — how to get the premium foldable for as cheap as possible\nStep aside, Samsung: there's a new foldable phone in town.\nThe preorder period has come to an end, but there are still a few Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold deals hanging around if you know where to look. From trade-in opportunities to free gift cards, keep reading for all of the best Pixel 11 Pro Fold deals on the web (so far).\nThe long-awaited Pixel 11 Pro Fold comes equipped with the new Tensor G6 processor, 16GB of RAM as standard, and one of the most advanced camera systems ever built into a foldable phone. It's also thinner and lighter than its predecessor while sporting a new reinforced hinge and IP68 durability straight out of the box.\nAt $1,899 for the 256GB configuration, the Pixel phone is also pretty expensive, which is why the following deals are so essential. Keep reading for the best offers so far, and don't forget to check back later: I'll keep adding new deals to this list as they go live.\nQuick links\n- The best Google Pixel 11 and Pixel 11 Pro deals\n- Verizon: Up to $1,100 off with trade-in, new line\n- T-Mobile: $900 off with most plans\n- Amazon: free $350 gift card with purchase\n- Best Buy: free $350 gift card with purchase\n- Google Store: Up to $1,000 off with trade-in\nGoogle Pixel 11 Pro Fold deals\nFAQ\nHow much does the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold cost?\nThe Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold starts at $1,899 for the 256GB configuration. That's obviously not cheap, but I was delighted to see that the foldable phone didn't receive a price increase this year (unlike some 2026 phones). All Pixel 11 series devices also come with six free months of the Google AI Pro plan.\nHow does the Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold compare to other foldable phones?\nThe Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold is being presented as the ultimate multitasking device, coming complete with the new Tensor G6 processor, 16GB of RAM, and useful productivity features like Split Screen and Drag & Drop.\nYou get two gorgeous Super Actua displays that are 20% brighter than last year's Pixel 10 Pro Fold, plus an upgraded hinge, scratch-resistant glass, and a design that's 10% lighter than the previous generation. The Google Pixel 11 Pro Fold is also equipped with an upgraded battery that's supposed to last up to 30 hours on a single charge.\nThese are some bold claims from Google, but we'll need to test the phone ourselves before we can attest to their veracity. If they're accurate, the Pixel 11 Pro Fold might be the best foldable phone that the company has ever produced.\nGet the latest news from Android Central, your trusted companion in the world of Android\nAfter almost a decade of working in the e-commerce space, Patrick Farmer (he/him) began his career at Android Central as a Deals and Commerce Writer before moving into a new role as AC's eCommerce Editor in 2023. When he's not hunting down the best deals and offering shopping advice for our readers, you'll often find him listening to music, camping out at a brewery, or treating his cat like a human child.\nYou must confirm your public display name before commenting\nPlease logout and then login again, you will then be prompted to enter your display name.",
