        "full_content": "Azerbaijan’s exports to Uzbekistan more than doubled in value\nBaku, August 21, AZERTAC\nIn January–July 2026, Azerbaijan’s exports to Uzbekistan amounted to $79.507 million, marking a 2.2-fold increase, or $44.130 million, compared with the corresponding period of last year, the State Customs Committee reported.\nDuring the reporting period, Azerbaijan imported $121.227 million worth of products from Uzbekistan, representing a 48% decrease, or $112.31 million, compared with the same period last year.\nAccording to the report, these figures accounted for 0.41 percent of Azerbaijan’s total exports and 1.23 percent of its imports.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\n- 21.08.2026 [18:36]\n® PASHA Holding continues to support projects implemented by ABAD\n- 21.08.2026 [18:19]\nBitcoin surpasses $77,000 for 1st time since May\n- 21.08.2026 [17:25]\nAzerbaijani journalists explore Sea Breeze Uzbekistan project\n- 21.08.2026 [15:57]\nAzerbaijan triples crude oil exports to Switzerland\n- 21.08.2026 [14:47]\n® Azercell wins three Brandon Hall Group HCM Excellence Awards®\n- 21.08.2026 [12:47]\nSOCAR opens applications for WIN Open Innovation Program\n- 21.08.2026 [12:22]\nAnother shipment sent to Armenia in transit via Azerbaijan\nEuroVolley 2026 Women: Azerbaijan beat Portugal in group C opener\n- 21.08.2026 [23:56]\nAzerbaijani boxers claim two European medals\n- 21.08.2026 [20:04]\nTop stories update\n- 21.08.2026 [20:00]\nBaku hosts opening ceremony of EuroVolley 2026 Women\n- 21.08.2026 [19:43]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Khojavend district\n- 21.08.2026 [19:06]\nAzerbaijani, Kyrgyz Supreme Courts to enhance partnership\n- 21.08.2026 [19:04]\nAzerbaijan’s exports to Uzbekistan more than doubled in value\n- 21.08.2026 [18:58]\n® PASHA Holding continues to support projects implemented by ABAD\n- 21.08.2026 [18:36]\nPrince Harry and others face multi-million pound bill over failed lawsuit\n- 21.08.2026 [18:21]\nBitcoin surpasses