        "full_content": "Azerbaijani, Kyrgyz Supreme Courts to enhance partnership\nBaku, August 21, AZERTAC\nIn addition to benefiting from Azerbaijan's experience in digitalization of the judicial system, Kyrgyzstan is also interested in further enhancing cooperation in this regard, Nurlan Alisherovich Musaev, Deputy Chairman of the Supreme Court of Kyrgyzstan, who is on a visit to Baku, said in an exclusive interview with AZERTAC.\nHe noted that he had formally requested the leadership of Azerbaijan’s Supreme Court to maintain long-term cooperation in this area.\nThe Kyrgyz Deputy Chairman empahsized that as part of the visit, they had also familiarized themselves with the efforts undertaken, decisions adopted and solutions applied in the country’s judicial system, as well as digital transformation and electronic judicial proceedings.\nNurlan Alisherovich Musaev described their visit to Azerbaijan as highly productive.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\nEuroVolley 2026 Women: Azerbaijan beat Portugal in group C opener\n- 21.08.2026 [23:56]\nAzerbaijani boxers claim two European medals\n- 21.08.2026 [20:04]\nTop stories update\n- 21.08.2026 [20:00]\nBaku hosts opening ceremony of EuroVolley 2026 Women\n- 21.08.2026 [19:43]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Khojavend district\n- 21.08.2026 [19:06]\nAzerbaijani, Kyrgyz Supreme Courts to enhance partnership\n- 21.08.2026 [19:04]\nAzerbaijan’s exports to Uzbekistan more than doubled in value\n- 21.08.2026 [18:58]\n® PASHA Holding continues to support projects implemented by ABAD\n- 21.08.2026 [18:36]\nPrince Harry and others face multi-million pound bill over failed lawsuit\n- 21.08.2026 [18:21]\nBitcoin surpasses $77,000 for 1st time since May\n- 21.08.2026 [18:19]\nBaku hosts international conference on Belgium’s colonialism\n- 21.08.2026 [18:16]\nAzerbaijan’s volleyball referee to officiate at EuroVolley 2026 Women\n- 21.08.2026 [18:01]\nAzerbaijani journalists explore Sea Breeze Uzbekistan project\n-