        "full_content": "Landmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Khojavend district\nBaku, August 21, AZERTAC\n“A mine incident occurred in the village of Dudukchu in the liberated Khojavend district on August 21,” the Ministry of Internal Affairs, the Prosecutor General’s Office, and the Mine Action Agency (ANAMA) said in a joint statement.\nAccording to the statement, a tractor operated by Ramal Giyas oghlu Shirinov, a 1983-born resident of Sumgayit, hit a mine in an area where demining activities were still underway. Shirinov sustained multiple injuries in the incident.\nThe Khojavend District Prosecutor’s Office is conducting an investigation into the incident.\nANAMA, the Ministry of Internal Affairs, and the Prosecutor General’s Office urged citizens to comply with safety rules, heed mine warning signs, and avoid unfamiliar areas.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\nEuroVolley 2026 Women: Azerbaijan beat Portugal in group C opener\n- 21.08.2026 [23:56]\nAzerbaijani boxers claim two European medals\n- 21.08.2026 [20:04]\nTop stories update\n- 21.08.2026 [20:00]\nBaku hosts opening ceremony of EuroVolley 2026 Women\n- 21.08.2026 [19:43]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Khojavend district\n- 21.08.2026 [19:06]\nAzerbaijani, Kyrgyz Supreme Courts to enhance partnership\n- 21.08.2026 [19:04]\nAzerbaijan’s exports to Uzbekistan more than doubled in value\n- 21.08.2026 [18:58]\n® PASHA Holding continues to support projects implemented by ABAD\n- 21.08.2026 [18:36]\nPrince Harry and others face multi-million pound bill over failed lawsuit\n- 21.08.2026 [18:21]\nBitcoin surpasses $77,000 for 1st time since May\n- 21.08.2026 [18:19]\nBaku hosts international conference on Belgium’s colonialism\n- 21.08.2026 [18:16]\nAzerbaijan’s volleyball referee to officiate at EuroVolley 2026 Women\n- 21.08.2026 [18:01]\nAzerbaijani journalists explore Sea Breeze Uzbekistan project\n- 21.08.2026 [17:25]\nWorld’s oldest person celebrates 117th birthday in UK\n- 21.08.