        "full_content": "Kyrgyzstan to benefit from Azerbaijan’s judicial experience, says Supreme Court Deputy Chairman\nBaku, August 21, AZERTAC\nKyrgyzstan intends to benefit from Azerbaijan’s experience in the development and implementation of the “Electronic Court” information system, Nurlan Alisherovich Musaev, Deputy Chairman of the Supreme Court of Kyrgyzstan, told AZERTAC during his visit to Baku.\nHighlighting Azerbaijan’s considerable progress in developing its “Electronic Court” information system, he added: “Recognizing these achievements, we reached out to our Azerbaijani colleagues, who gave us an opportunity to familiarize ourselves with their digitalization efforts. During our visit, we visited the Supreme Court, Narimanov District Court, and Baku Court of Appeal, where we saw firsthand how digital services operate.”\n“Although many services have been introduced, they remain largely fragmented. We sought to draw on Azerbaijan’s experience in integrating digital solutions across the judicial system. We have gained valuable experience here and believe we will put it into practice in Kyrgyzstan,” he emphasized.\nFEEDBACK\nOther news in this section\n- 21.08.2026 [20:00]\nTop stories update\n- 21.08.2026 [19:04]\nAzerbaijani, Kyrgyz Supreme Courts to enhance partnership\n- 21.08.2026 [12:00]\nTop stories update\nEuroVolley 2026 Women: Azerbaijan beat Portugal in group C opener\n- 21.08.2026 [23:56]\nAzerbaijani boxers claim two European medals\n- 21.08.2026 [20:04]\nTop stories update\n- 21.08.2026 [20:00]\nBaku hosts opening ceremony of EuroVolley 2026 Women\n- 21.08.2026 [19:43]\nLandmine blast injures one in Azerbaijan’s Khojavend district\n- 21.08.2026 [19:06]\nAzerbaijani, Kyrgyz Supreme Courts to enhance partnership\n- 21.08.2026 [19:04]\nAzerbaijan’s exports to Uzbekistan more than doubled in value\n- 21.08.2026 [18:58]\n® PASHA Holding continues to support projects implemented by ABAD\n- 21.08.2026 [18:36]\nPrince Harry and others face multi-mil