        "full_content": "'ZDNET Recommends': What exactly does it mean?\nZDNET's recommendations are based on many hours of testing, research, and comparison shopping. We gather data from the best available sources, including vendor and retailer listings as well as other relevant and independent reviews sites. And we pore over customer reviews to find out what matters to real people who already own and use the products and services we’re assessing.\nWhen you click through from our site to a retailer and buy a product or service, we may earn affiliate commissions. This helps support our work, but does not affect what we cover or how, and it does not affect the price you pay. Neither ZDNET nor the author are compensated for these independent reviews. Indeed, we follow strict guidelines that ensure our editorial content is never influenced by advertisers.\nZDNET's editorial team writes on behalf of you, our reader. Our goal is to deliver the most accurate information and the most knowledgeable advice possible in order to help you make smarter buying decisions on tech gear and a wide array of products and services. Our editors thoroughly review and fact-check every article to ensure that our content meets the highest standards. If we have made an error or published misleading information, we will correct or clarify the article. If you see inaccuracies in our content, please report the mistake via this form.\nThe best early Labor Day 2026 TV deals: Samsung, LG, and more\nLabor Day is your last chance for summer cookouts and celebrations before cooler autumn weather rolls in and the kids head back to school. And while TVs might not be the first thing you think of when it comes to Labor Day sales, it's a great time to pick up a budget-friendly model for your dorm room or splurge on a high-end upgrade for your home theater.\nAlso: The LG C6 OLED TV is one of the most impressive TVs I've tested year - and it's on sale\nRight now at Best Buy, you can take advantage of steep discounts on TVs from brands like LG, Sony, and Hisense during the retailer's 60th-anniversary sale. But you'll have to hurry, the sale ends this Sunday -- and with deals like these, stock is sure to sell out fast.\nAlso: We lab-tested 7 TVs for color accuracy - and the winners weren't Sony or Samsung\nBest early Labor Day 2026 TV deals\n- Current price: $5,500 (15% off)\n- Regular price: $6,500\nI got to test out the R95H in the Louisville lab and was very impressed by the color accuracy it produced. The new Micro RGB panel works similarly to an OLED, giving you pixel-level dimming for ultra-sharp detailing and near-perfect black contrast.\nReview: Samsung R95H Micro RGB\n- Current price: $1,700 (37% off)\n- Regular price: $2,700\nThe LG C6 OLED has plenty of updates for this year's flagship refresh, including LG Shield privacy, a Dynamic Sports picture mode, and an OLED screen care feature to protect picture quality.\nReview: LG C6 OLED\n- Current price: $1,400 (44% off)\n- Regular price: $2,500\nOne of my favorite TCL TVs got a major upgrade this year with its own version of the new Micro RGB technology. Not only does it drastically improve color accuracy and visual appeal, it also gives the TV a brightness boost with a max of 6,000 nits (compared to the 5,000 nit max of its predecessors).\nReview: TCL QM8L SQD-Mini LED\n- Current price: $999 (56% off)\n- Regular price: $2,300\nThis cinema-sized screen offers a 144Hz refresh rate, Dolby Vision HDR, Dolby Atmos virtual surround sound, and dedicated picture modes for film buffs and serious console gamers.\nRead more: The best 98-inch TVs\n- Current price: $360 (60% off)\n- Regular price: $900\nA great entry-level Mini LED TV with 4K resolution, a 60Hz refresh rate, Dolby Atmos and Dolby Vision support, and built-in Alexa voice controls.\nAlso: Get better color accuracy on your TV with these simple steps\nMore early Labor Day TV deals\n- LG C5 OLED 65-inch: $1,500 (save $1,200): Last year's flagship OLED still offers