        "link": "http://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/w3ct8jss",
        "source": "Discovery",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:05:23.145857+00:00",
        "image": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/images/ic/1200x675/p0kxnch7.jpg",
        "full_content": "Women Not Included: Safety Equipment\nIn a world not designed for women, safety equipment – from PPE to car crash testing – reveals how protection standards built on male bodies can leave women exposed.\nSafety equipment is often designed around an “average” male body and Dr Ella Hubber wants to understand the consequences this has for women. Alongside journalist Candice Bailey and expert voices, we hear how healthcare workers are forced to adapt to PPE never made for them and how car safety systems fail to reflect the way women’s bodies respond in collisions.\nAs awareness grows, they also ask what change can look like and if, through better data, and more women’s input, safety equipment can protect us all equally.\nPresenter/Producer: Ella Hubber\nResearcher: Elliott Prince\nEditor: Ilan Goodman\nOn radio\nMore episodes\nFeatured\n- \n    .\nBroadcasts\n- Monday 19:32GMTBBC World Service\n- Tuesday 04:32GMTBBC World Service Australasia, Americas and the Caribbean, South Asia & East Asia only\n- Tuesday 12:32GMTBBC World Service Australasia, East and Southern Africa, News Internet & West and Central Africa only\n- Monday 00:32GMTBBC World Service & Live News\nThe Curious Cases of Rutherford and Fry\nPodcast\n- \n                                        DiscoveryExplorations in the world of science.",
