        "full_content": "Assam floods: What turned a safe village into a disaster zone?\nIn July, villages in Upper Assam that had never seen a flood before went under water.\n“Everything got washed away in a matter of hours,” said Mahesh Barhoi, a resident of Nepalikhuti village in Assam’s Sivasagar district, near the border with Nagaland.\nWhen devastating floods swept through the district in July, they left a trail of destruction by killing nearly 50 people and wiping out entire villages like Nepalikhuti.\nWhile Assam battles floods every year, the July catastrophe was different – Nepalikhuti had never seen a flood before.\nWhat caused this unprecedented flood?\nHow is it connected to illegal mining?\nWe travelled to Assam and Nagaland to find out.\nWatch our ground report.",
