        "title": "Who’s winning AI search in Fintech? Leaders pulling ahead across five categories",
        "link": "https://www.fintechnews.org/whos-winning-ai-search-in-fintech-leaders-pulling-ahead-across-five-categories/",
        "source": "fintechnews.org",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:05:23.144556+00:00",
        "image": "https://www.fintechnews.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Fintech-1.jpg",
        "full_content": "New AIVx Report data across Digital Banks, Payments, Digital Assets, WealthTech, and Alternative Investments shows third-party sources dominate AI citations while category leaders capture outsized visibility\nAvenue Z, a digital marketing and PR agency specializing in AI search visibility and AEO, today released its latest AI Visibility Index Report findings across five fintech categories: Digital Banks, Payments, Digital Assets, WealthTech, and Alts.\nTogether, the latest AIVx reports show a clear pattern emerging across fintech: AI search visibility is increasingly shaped by third-party authority, and a relatively small group of brands are pulling away in each category – specifically:\n- Fintech: Digital Banks\n  - SoFi leads digital banks, where the top five brands – SoFi, Chime, Ally, Capital One, and Varo – control 66.0% of AI citations, reinforcing that the brands winning AI search are the ones the market already talks about most – a battle won through the strategic execution of editorial media and content dissemination. See the full AIVx Digital Banks report for more.\n- Fintech: Payments\n  - Stripe leads Payments, where the top five brands – Stripe, PayPal, Adyen, Square, and Venmo – control 90.0% of AI citations. This reinforces that in the Payments category, AI visibility is highly concentrated, with the top two brands establishing clear separation from the broader competitive field. See the full AIVx Payments Report report for more.\n- Fintech: Digital Assets\n  - Fireblocks leads digital assets, where the top five brands – Fireblocks, Coinbase, BitGo, Anchorage Digital, and Copper – only control 38.0% of AI citations, showing a market that remains more open while third-party authority already separates the leaders. Similar to other categories the battle in digital assets is being won by brands that consistently dominate earned media and thought-leadership content. View the AIVx Digital Assets Report report for more.\n- Fintech: WealthTech\n  - Envestnet leads the WealthTech category, where the top five brands – Envestnet, Addepar, Black Diamond, Redtail, and Advyzon – control 55.0% of AI citations, showing a competitive field that is still taking shape, and unlike other categories in the fintech space, AI visibility in WealthTech is being shaped by the sources that help buyers compare and validate providers. View the complete AIVx WealthTech Report full report for more.\n- Fintech: Alts\n  - iCapital leads the Alts category, where the top five brands – iCapital, Yieldstreet, CAIS, Moonfare, and Fundrise – hold 64.0% of AI citations, demonstrating a category that is beginning to consolidate around a small set of leaders, while Alts brands still have the opportunity to gain AI visibility through third-party authority and more reusable content signals. See the full AIVx Alts Report report for more.\nAmong the third-party sources noted for their impact in driving AI visibility, top-tier editorial media and trade publications were found to be especially effective. The AIVx reports state that these editorial environments help set the recommendation layer, but do not dominate the category on their own; the strongest visibility profiles are built by brands that show up across trade coverage, business press, company information pages, and reference environments at the same time. Editorial media and trade publications found to have the most impact by retrievals were: Forbes, The Wall Street Journal, Barrons, Reuters, TechRepublic, TechRadar, InvestmentNews, and BeInCrypto, among others.\n“AI trusts the entire signal around your brand more than any one channel, including your own website,” said Whitney Hart, CSO and Director of the AI Lab at Avenue Z. “Across fintech, the brands winning AI visibility are the ones treating PR, editorial coverage, reference sources, and owned content as one system: they earn third-party validation, structure their sites so AI models can actually use it, and build content that shows how they solve real problems in the category rather than just repeating their tagline.”\nAs brands compete for influence in AI search, Avenue Z’s AIVx reports provide a category-by-category benchmark for where visibility is being won, how citation authority is formed, and which brands are setting the pace. The findings suggest that the window is still open, but narrowing, for fintech brands that want to build durable AI visibility before the market leaders widen the gap further.\n“It’s validating to see that our AIVx data reiterates that editorial authority is a key pillar of AI search viability,” said Libbie Wilcox, Vice President of PR, and Managing Director of Avenue Z’s New York City Office. “The companies leading the AI visibility race are the ones who prioritize traditional PR. They have built out thought leadership programs and a steady stream of coverage across a wide range of outlets, from tier-one to trade media. They’re coupling these efforts and outputs with strong owned-content programs designed around specific AI search prompts and their priority LLMs. That level of consideration is clearly making a difference.”\n“Building on that, seeing Forbes, WSJ, Barrons, TechRadar, and niche fintech publications show up again and again in our AIVx reports is energizing for our PR teams, but it also raises the bar,” said Bristol Jones, Vice President of PR, and Managing Director of Avenue Z’s Miami Office. “Fintech brands need a PR program that knows which editorial environments actually move AI visibility, how to pitch stories that align with target AI prompts, and how to manage sentiment and accuracy across all third-party coverage.”",
        "content": "New AIVx Report data across Digital Banks, Payments, Digital Assets, WealthTech, and Alternative Investments shows third-party sources dominate AI citations while category leaders capture outsized visibility\nAvenue Z, a digital marketing and PR agency specializing in AI search visibility and AEO, today released its latest AI Visibility Index Report findings across five fintech categories: Digital ...",
