        "title": "Danish expression of the day: at gøre sig umage",
        "link": "https://www.thelocal.dk/20260820/danish-expression-of-the-day-at-gore-sig-umage",
        "source": "The Local Denmark",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:05:23.144514+00:00",
        "image": "https://assets.thelocal.com/cdn-cgi/rs:fit:1200/quality:75/plain/https://apiwp.thelocal.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/watermarks-logo-word-of-the-day-template-13.jpg@webp",
        "full_content": "What does At gøre sig umage mean?\nThe expression translates directly to “to make an effort” or “to do your best”. However the word umage doesn’t have an exact translation to English, and this is what gives it a slightly deeper nuance. At gøre sig umage has a subtle added meaning of diligence and attention to detail and precision. When you gør dig umage, you really care about the quality of the outcome.\nWhere does At gøre sig umage come from?\nThe word umage originates from the Middle Low German word ungemak, which directly translates to \"trouble,\" \"hardship,\" or \"discomfort\". It is a negated form of the root word mag (which means comfort or ease).\nHistorically, the expression meant to strain yourself or to cause yourself trouble or discomfort in order to achieve the results possible. It has since then evolved to mean a sense of deliberate, caring effort.\nWhy is at gøre sig umage worth knowing?\nTaking time to do things properly is considered to be quite a Danish trait - hence the country's reputation for design and craftsmanship. At gøre sig umage is therefore a term which pops up frequently in the Danish language. It can come from your manager at work, or may be a way to praise a child who has made a real effort.\nExamples\nDu skal gøre dig umage med dine lektier, hvis du vil have gode karakterer.\n“You need to make a real effort with your homework if you want good marks.”\nHold da op, hvor har du gjort dig umage med maden i aften!\n“Wow, you made a real effort with the food tonight!”\nDet er lige meget, om du vinder, så længe du bare gør dig umage.\n“It doesn't matter if you win, as long as you just do your best.”",
