        "full_content": "Prices in this month's price comparison are relatively unchanged compared to July. This is mainly due to Føtex and Bilka adding new low-cost options to their assortment.\nLidl for the fourth month running steals the show, with the cheapest products in 7 out of 8 categories.\nRema 1000 is close behind, followed by online supermarket, Nemlig.com.\nNetto takes 4th place, with a slight increase in prices.\nOverall, meat and fish have become cheaper, while sweets, snacks, ice cream and drinks have become more expensive.\nThe price difference between the cheapest and most expensive shopping basket is 23 percent.\nThe cheapest shopping basket is from Lidl, with a price of 2,047 kroner.\nThe most expensive is from Meny, at 2,519 kroner per shopping basket.\nFøtex has seen the biggest price change, going from 2,319 kroner in July, to 2,291 kroner in August, resulting in it jumping three spots, from 10th place to 7th place, in just a month.\nEach basket consists of approximately 100 products from eight different categories: fruits and veg, bread and cakes, meat and fish, dry goods and pantry staples, dairy products, sweets, frozen items, and drinks.",
