        "full_content": "Turnstile Enlist Elton John, Hayley Williams, Slayyyter for ‘Never Enough: Versions’ LP\nTurnstile have enlisted artists like Elton John, Hayley Williams, Slayyyter, A.G. Cook and more for a “reimagined” take on their 2025 album Never Enough.\nNever Enough: Versions, out August 28, features the aforementioned artists plus a diverse array of guests including Panda Bear, Blood Orange, Julien Baker, Dying Fetus, Four Tet, Alex G, Faye Webster and others remaking the hardcore band’s Best Rock Album Grammy-winning LP.\nAlso on the guest list are Oklou, Shabaka, fellow Baltimore native Dan Deacon, Porches, Floating Points, Brandon Woody, Chanel Beads, Angel Du$t, Nourished By Time, Rod Lee, Kettama, and Mustafa.\nIt’s unclear whether the artists involved are simply guesting on Turnstile’s remakes or contributing their own covers; fans will find out when Never Enough: Versions arrives one week from today.\nSome of the contributing artists — Angel Du$t, Nourished by Time, Slayyyter, and Porches — will also take part in Turnstile’s Never Enough Tour Pt. 2, which brings a mini-festival to amphitheaters nationwide this September and October. The trek kicks off September 9 in Milwaukee and concludes a month later in Santa Ana, California on October 18.\nOther artists joining Turnstile along the way at select stops include Clipse, Vince Staples, Haywire, Terror, Hatebreed, Thundercat, Saya Gray, Die Spitz and more.",
