        "title": "Tomb Raider I-III Remastered Update Adds Three New Features, Includes 60fps In Classic Graphics Mode",
        "link": "https://www.nintendolife.com/news/2026/08/tomb-raider-i-iii-remastered-update-adds-three-new-features-includes-60fps-in-classic-graphics-mode",
        "source": "Nintendo Life | Latest Updates",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:05:23.143494+00:00",
        "image": "https://images.nintendolife.com/b1122c75bc68e/large.jpg",
        "full_content": "Aspyr recently revived The Lord of the Rings: War in the North, and this week it returns to Tomb Raider I-III Remastered with a community patch, adding some requested features.\nThis update includes three new features across all versions of the game and also comes loaded optimisations and bug fixes for the Switch 2 version. The new features include a brightness slider, a pickup highlight, and 60fps in classic graphics mode.\nHere's the official rundown via Aspyr's support page:\nTomb Raider I-III Remastered: Challenge Mode Patch 3: Community Update\nNEW FEATURES\nAll Platforms\n- Brightness Slider: Change the brightness of any level across all 3 games (best results with intended use in HD Graphics Mode).\n- 60 FPS in Classic Graphics Mode: Framerate is now 60 fps in Classic for a seamless gameplay experience on any console.\n- Pickup Highlight: Key items Lara can pick up are now brighter and more visible in HD Graphics Mode.\nBUG FIXES\nMultiple Platforms\n- Fixed a clipping issue in Natla's Mines where the character could pass through the boat.\n- Fixed a UI bug where harpoon gun ammo counts were not displayed.\n- Added missing descriptions for several modifiers in Challenge Mode.\n- Fixed a physics issue in the Living Quarters where Lara remained hanging in the air.\n- Fixed a visual rendering issue in Tomb of Tihocan where boulders would flicker in and out of view.\n- Improved the reliability of executing a running Swan Dive when using touch controls.\n- Fixed a grab-mechanic issue in The Cistern level for ledges.\n- Fixed an issue where inverse controller settings were not applied correctly.\n- Changed the default value for \"Retro FPS\" to enabled across all applicable platforms.\n- Improved ladder mounting mechanics in the Opera House level.\n- Fixed a sequence breaking issue in Atlantis where backflipping with Tank Controls bypassed lighting triggers.\n- Fixed a bug where the last used Challenge Mode outfit incorrectly persisted in normal levels and Lara's Home.\n- Corrected a tooltip error regarding game completion requirements for the Golden Pistols.\n- Fixed a bug preventing Photo Mode from opening correctly without extra input.\n- Fixed a collision issue in the City of Khamoon where Lara could fall through a half-opened trapdoor.\nSwitch 2\n- Fixed an issue in St. Francis Folly where Lara and lions could become stuck in corners.\n- Fixed a softlock in Highland Fling caused by Lara getting stuck after jumping onto a rock.\n- Fixed environmental clipping issues involving the T-Rex upon its defeat.\n- Fixed a collision bug allowing characters to clip through the Cargo Plane’s cockpit.\n- Fixed flickering \"Goo\" textures in Room 3 of the Reunion level while in Classic Mode.\n- Fixed flickering textures in the Shakespeare Cliff secret area while in Classic Mode.\n- Fixed missing enemy spawns in the Caves of Kaliya when utilizing type modifiers.\n- Fixed glitched enemy spawns in Lud's Gate when using the randomizer.\n- Fixed an issue in the Crash Site where the airplane cargo door failed to open.\n- Fixed a softlock where the T-Rex bite failed to trigger a death screen.\nTomb Raider I-III Remastered originally launched for the Switch in 2024 and was followed by a Switch 2 release earlier this year. This includes a free upgrade for existing Switch owners.\nAs a reminder, Aspyr's revival of The Lord of the Rings: War in the North is now also available in Europe on the Switch and Switch 2. It was released earlier this month in North America and other locations.",
        "content": "Aspyr recently revived The Lord of the Rings: War in the North, and this week it returns to Tomb Raider I-III Remastered with a community patch, adding some requested features.\nThis update includes three new features across all versions of the game and also comes loaded optimisations and bug fixes for the Switch 2 version. The new features include a brightness slider, a pickup highlight, and 60fps...",
