        "image": "https://images.nintendolife.com/86ef4962730c3/large.jpg",
        "full_content": "Minecraft Dungeons II is gearing up for its official launch on the Switch and Switch 2 next month.\nAhead of release, the team at Mojang has released an official gameplay trailer showcasing this new action-packed experience, as well as mysterious rifts, which lead to the Sift - a new dimension introducing powerful threats and all sorts of landscapes.\nAlong the way, you'll also face new foes, team up with friends, customise gear and engage in all sorts of explosive battles.\n\"Ever since we announced Minecraft Dungeons II, we’ve seen mysterious rifts open in various locations. Until now, we could only speculate about what lies beyond them. Where do they lead, and what can brave adventurers expect to find there?\n\"We finally have our answer. Players who step through the rifts will enter the Sift, an entirely new dimension coming to Minecraft Dungeons II! This dimension is equally strange and beautiful, bringing powerful and mysterious threats as well as landscapes that will stop you in your tracks. Take a closer look in the gameplay trailer.\"\nPre-orders are now live for this new action RPG adventure, with the game arriving on 29th September 2026. This release will follow the first Minecraft Dungeons, which launched on the Switch in 2020 and received all sorts of updates and DLC.",
