        "image": "https://images.nintendolife.com/24272e978f376/large.jpg",
        "full_content": "Nintendo's music app for Switch Online members has today been updated with the SimCity SNES soundtrack.\nThis version of Will Wright's city-building hit was released on the Super Nintendo in 1991. Nintendo published the title and also helped Maxis with this version of the game.\nThe soundtrack, composed by Soyo Oka (Super Mario Kart), contains 21 songs and has a runtime of 23 minutes. It's worth noting this game isn't actually available for the Switch Online's 'Nintendo Classics' SNES library. The title was previously released on the Virtual Console during the Wii generation and eventually got removed.\nIf there are any significant updates about the game's availability on Nintendo platforms and services, we'll let you know. For now, here's every song included in this latest update for Nintendo Music:\nSimCity - SNES (21st Aug 2026)\n- Title Screen\n- Menu\n- Village\n- Dr. Wright\n- Urban Expansion\n- Town\n- City Evaluation (Bad)\n- Gift\n- Amusement Park\n- City Evaluation (Good)\n- City\n- Fiscal Budget (Japanese Ver.)\n- Capital\n- Disaster\n- Game Over\n- Metropolis\n- Scenario Clear\n- Megalopolis\n- Mario Statue Erected\n- Population of 600,000\n- Save Complete\nThis follows an update for Nintendo Music earlier this week, which added the Super Mario 3D Land and Super Mario 3D World Free Roam soundtracks from Mario Kart World.\nMario Kart World - Switch 2 (17th Aug 2026)\nFree Roam with Super Mario 3D Land\n- Ground Theme\n- Beach Theme (Jazz)\n- Beach Theme (Bossa Nova)\n- Snow Mountain Theme\nFree Roam with Super Mario 3D World\n- Super Bell Hill\n- Shifty Boo\n- Captain Toad (Goes Forth)\n- Athletic Theme (Jazz)\n- Atheletic Theme (Soul)\n- Hisstocrat\n- Sprawling Savanna\n- Bowser's Highway\n- Doule Cherry Pass\n- Hands-On Hall\n- Piranha Creeper Creek\n- World 8\n- Plessie Ride!\n- Attack! Bowser's Fury",
