    {
        "title": "Deployment Storage keeps your deployments rollback-ready",
        "link": "https://vercel.com/changelog/deployment-storage-keeps-your-deployments-rollback-ready",
        "source": "Vercel News",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:05:23.142771+00:00",
        "image": "https://assets.vercel.com/image/upload/contentful/image/e5382hct74si/gsSX6ZVmOUoz2eg9XIbJh/0798a6d3b19f95fd1fe01c275e6c7c68/image.png",
        "full_content": "Every deployment produces a set of files, including the pages, functions, and assets Vercel serves. Deployment Storage keeps those files available so you can inspect previous deployments and roll back when needed.\nInstantly roll back to previous deployments in seconds\nIf a production deploy ships a bug or a change you want to reverse, rolling back restores the previous version in seconds. Open your project, click Instant Rollback on the Production Deployment tile, then choose an earlier production deployment. Vercel immediately repoints your domains to that deployment, with no rebuild required.\nDeployment Storage pricing\n- Deployment Storage is billed at $0.10 per GB per month\n- Hobby teams include up to 10 GB\nExisting teams continue with their current pricing, with no change to their bill at this time.\nControl how much Deployment Storage you keep:\n- Edit your Deployment Retention Policy to set how long Pre-Production, Production, Canceled, and Errored deployments stay available. Shorter retention means less storage, but you can't roll back to a deleted deployment\n- The Usage page shows Deployment Storage and Functions Storage by project\n- Keep future deployments smaller by trimming your output directory, moving large files to Vercel Blob, and reducing Function bundle size\nLearn more about Deployment Storage here.",
        "content": "Every deployment produces a set of files, including the pages, functions, and assets Vercel serves. Deployment Storage keeps those files available so you can inspect previous deployments and roll back when needed.\nInstantly roll back to previous deployments in seconds\nIf a production deploy ships a bug or a change you want to reverse, rolling back restores the previous version in seconds. Open you...",
        "tags": [
            "General"
        ],
        "location": "Global",
        "human_time": "1h ago"
