        "title": "More headroom, a lower per-credit rate, and a bill you can predict: introducing new Pro plan tiers",
        "link": "https://www.netlify.com/blog/new-pro-plan-tiers",
        "source": "Netlify Blog",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T21:05:23.141838+00:00",
        "image": "https://cdn.sanity.io/images/o0o2tn5x/production/d0354fe52c160a3abdfdeff297a1baf090302a3d-1600x900.png",
        "full_content": "Today we’re introducing four additional tiers for the Netlify Pro plan.\nNow teams on the Pro plan can get up to 20,000 monthly plan credits for a single flat price, making it easier to choose the right level that matches how you actually use Netlify. When you move to one of the higher tiers, your effective cost per credit also decreases, helping you save compared to purchasing additional credits on demand.\nIf your current Pro plan already fits your needs, nothing changes. These new tiers are completely optional.\nMore predictable monthly statements, plus some savings\nOne of the most common pieces of feedback we’ve heard from Pro customers is that credit usage can vary from month to month. That’s one of the strengths of usage-based billing (since it scales with how you use the platform), but the variability can make monthly statements harder to predict.\nThe new Pro tiers make that easier.\nInstead of juggling extra credit packs, you can select a tier that better matches your typical usage and pay one consistent monthly price. If your needs grow, moving to one of the higher tiers also lowers your effective cost per credit.\nEven better, credits included with the new tiers roll over into your next billing cycle, giving you additional flexibility when usage naturally fluctuates.\nCredits that roll over automatically\nThe 10,000, 15,000, and 20,000 credit tiers have an extra benefit: any unused credits from your current billing cycle will automatically roll over into the next one.\nThat gives extra time to use each credit, helping you absorb spikes in usage. (Each credit on the new higher tiers can be used the month it’s granted plus one additional billing period. Credits included with the base 3,000 credit tier do not roll over.)\nSo should you upgrade?\nThe new Pro tiers provide three practical benefits for accounts that have high usage or experience seasonal surges:\n- Lower effective cost: Higher tiers reduce your effective price per credit compared to purchasing additional credits as needed.\n- More predictable billing: Match your monthly credit allotment to your expected usage and simplify your monthly invoice.\n- More flexibility: Rolled-over credits give you room to absorb temporary spikes without immediately purchasing additional credits.\nSee the new plans\nWe’ve updated our pricing page with the new Pro tiers and they are now available to existing accounts in your Netlify dashboard.\nNothing changes unless you want it to\nThese new tiers are entirely opt-in.\nIf you’re happy with your current Pro plan, you don’t need to do anything.\n- Your existing Pro plan, credit balance, credit packs, and auto recharges continue to work exactly as they do today.\n- Free, Personal, and Enterprise plans are unaffected.\nWhether you’re looking for more headroom, more predictable billing, or better value at higher usage levels, the new Pro tiers give you another way to match Netlify to the way your team builds and ships web sites and applications.",
